ss of who wrote first:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"// paddingTop wins for the top side, wherever it was written.\n<div sx={[css({ paddingTop: \"2rem\" }), css({ padding: \"1rem\" })]} />","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// paddingTop wins for the top side, wherever it was written.</span>\n&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">div</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={[<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">paddingTop</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;2rem&quot;</span> }), <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">padding</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1rem&quot;</span> })]} /&gt;"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ambiguity-is-reported-not-guessed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ambiguity is reported, not guessed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When two entries for the same property could both match, set different values, and\nthe ladder cannot separate them, the compiler emits "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ambiguous-precedence","source":"ambiguous-precedence"}},{"type":"text","value":" rather\nthan picking one:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({\n  color: {\n    '[data-state=\"open\"]': \"red\",\n    \"[aria-expanded]\": \"blue\", // both can be true at once\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span>: {\n    <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&#39;[data-state=&quot;open&quot;]&#39;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;red&quot;</span>,\n    <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;[aria-expanded]&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;blue&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// both can be true at once</span>\n  },\n})"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three ways to resolve it:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nest the winner"}]},{"type":"text","value":" inside the loser. Two conditions beat one, and the\nambiguity is gone:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({\n  color: {\n    \"[aria-expanded]\": {\n      base: \"blue\",\n      '[data-state=\"open\"]': \"red\",\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span>: {\n    <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;[aria-expanded]&quot;</span>: {\n      <span class=\"th-token th-property\">base</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;blue&quot;</span>,\n      <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&#39;[data-state=&quot;open&quot;]&#39;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;red&quot;</span>,\n    },\n  },\n})"}}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Say they are exclusive."}]},{"type":"text","value":" When a library guarantees two attributes never\nappear together ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-string\">[data-open]</span>","source":"[data-open]"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-string\">[data-closed]</span>","source":"[data-closed]"}},{"type":"text","value":"), declare it once in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/reference/config","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"conditions.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">exclusive</span>","source":"conditions.exclusive"}}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the same value"}]},{"type":"text","value":", if that is the truth. Two entries with the same value\nare never ambiguous."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compiler already knows some pairs are exclusive on their own: two values of\none attribute, a selector and its negation, or two fixed positions counted from\nthe same end."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"combinations-that-cannot-match","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combinations that cannot match"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A key nested in another it can never meet, such as two values of one attribute or\ntwo libraries' states declared apart with\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/reference/config","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"conditions.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">exclusiveAcross</span>","source":"conditions.exclusiveAcross"}}]},{"type":"text","value":", matches no element. Its\nentries are left out of the stylesheet. A style written once for several libraries\ncan nest one state helper inside another without shipping rules nothing can match,\nand without a word from the compiler, since the configuration declared the libraries\napart. Any other such key is a mistake, and the compiler says so with an info,\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"unreachable-entry","source":"unreachable-entry"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"layers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Everything Kirana emits is inside layers, in this order:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"@layer reset, base, kirana; /* your layers, from configuration */\n@layer kirana.tokens, kirana.themes, kirana.contextual, kirana.atoms;","lang":"css","html":"@layer reset, base, kirana; <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">/* your layers, from configuration */</span>\n@layer kirana.tokens, kirana.themes, kirana.contextual, kirana.atoms;"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your own global CSS (a reset, base element styles) goes in layers you name in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/config/layers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":", which sit below every Kirana rule. Nothing\nKirana writes is unlayered, custom-property assignments included."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"asking-why","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Asking why"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a value does not win and you want the reason, ask:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"kirana-style trace src/components/card.tsx:24 padding-top","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> trace src/components/card.tsx:24 padding-top","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It prints one line per candidate declaration (value, conditions, layer), marks\nthe winner, and names the step that decided it, for example\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"step <span class=\"th-token th-number\">5</span> (<span 